# Rust
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.orig

# Tauri writes the capability JSON schemas here on every build. They are derived
# from the permissions the crate actually uses, so they are build output, not
# source — the checked-in thing is capabilities/default.json.
crates/tezca-settings/gen/

# tezca link backups (should never be committed)
*.bak.*
*.tezca-backup

# Editor / OS
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Design handoffs and the like arrive as archives and are unpacked in place. The
# unpacked tree is what gets read (and, when it is a spec worth keeping, tracked
# — see design_handoff_tezca_desktop/); the archive itself is never the artefact.
*.zip

# Machine-local state is NOT in this repo at all — it lives in ~/.config/tezca/ and
# in the real (un-symlinked) ~/.config/tezca-bar/ and ~/.config/tezca-dock/
# directories, so `tezca hypr set` / `keybind rebind` / `bar set` never dirty the
# tree. See DESIGN.md §4 principle 6 and §8.
#
# conf.d/local.conf stays tracked as a hand-editable stub (so Hyprland's `source`
# never errors on a fresh clone). Nothing writes to it — it is yours.
